nce inequality (1) is\nfalse, contradicting the assumed existence of a configuration with at most one sunny line.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Conclusion\n\nThe contradiction shows that any collection of \\(n\\) distinct lines covering all points of\n\\(T_{n}\\) must contain **at least two sunny lines**.  Therefore the set of admissible values\nof \\(k\\) satisfies\n\n\\[\nk\\in\\{2,3,\\dots ,n\\}.\n\\]\n\nThe existence of configurations for every \\(k\\ge 2\\) has not been established here; only the\nnecessary condition \\(k\\ge 2\\) has been proved. \u220e"
