e n\\bigr\\}.\n\\]\n\n*Number of lines.*  \nThe two sub\u2011collections are disjoint, hence  \n\n\\[\n|\\mathcal L| = k + (n-k)=n .\n\\]\n\n*Number of sunny lines.*  \nExactly the first \\(k\\) lines have slope \\(1\\); the remaining \\(n-k\\) lines are horizontal.  Therefore \\(\\mathcal L\\) contains precisely \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n*Coverage of required points.*  \nLet \\((a,b)\\in\\mathcal P\\).\n\n* If \\(b-a\\le k-1\\) then, by (2), \\((a,b)\\) lies on the sunny line \\(\\ell^{\\text{sun}}_{\\,b-a}\\in\\mathcal L\\).\n* If \\(b-a\\ge k\\) then \\((a,b)\\in T_k\\) by definition, and by (6) it lies on the horizontal line \\(\\ell^{\\text{hor}}_{b}\\in\\mathcal L\\).\n\nThus every point demanded by the problem belongs to at least one line of \\(\\mathcal L\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5. Extreme values of \\(k\\)\n\n* **\\(k=0\\).**  \n  The construction yields only the horizontal lines \\(y=1, y=2,\\dots ,y=n\\); none is sunny, and every point of \\(\\mathcal P\\) satisfies \\(b-a\\ge 0\\), so it lies on the appropriate horizontal line.\n\n* **\\(k=n\\).**  \n  The construction yields the \\(n\\) sunny lines \\(y=x, y=x+1,\\dots ,y=x+n-1\\); there are no horizontal lines, and every point of \\(\\mathcal P\\) satisfies \\(b-a\\le n-1\\), hence lies on one of them.\n\nBoth extremes are therefore admissible.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 6. Conclusion\n\nFor any integer \\(n\\ge 3\\) and any integer \\(k\\) with \\(0\\le k\\le n\\) we have exhibited an explicit set \\(\\mathcal L\\) of \\(n\\) distinct lines that\n\n* contain every lattice point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge 1\\) and \\(a+b\\le n+1\\);\n* contain exactly \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\nHence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is precisely  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,n\\}} .\n\\]\n\n\u220e\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
